sentences.l:
The fiery force of the vaulted and weightless sky
flashed out and made a place for itself in the topmost citadel;
nearest to it is air, in lightness and in place:

Of these, the one that is in the middle is not habitable, for the heat;
deep snow covers two; as many he set between each of the two
and gave a temperate blend by flame mixed with cold.

And lest any region should be bereft of its own living things,
the stars hold the heavenly floor, and the shapes of the gods;
the waters gave way to the gleaming fish, to be lived in;
the earth took the wild beasts, the restless air the birds.
